DESCRIPTION:World Peace Day turns up on November 17 in most American day-of
 -the-year listings\, and no founding organization\, government page\, or n
 ews report explains how it got there. The two peace observances that do ha
 ve documented origins fall elsewhere on the calendar: January 1\, proposed
  by Pope Paul VI in December 1967\, and September 21\, established by the 
 United Nations General Assembly. This page gives what the record supports 
 and leaves the November 17 date where the evidence leaves it.\n\nhttps://t
 odaycelebrates.com/holiday/world-peace-day/
